      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1189",
      "html": "<ul><li><strong>Scientific name:</strong> Pseudopimelodus schultzi (Dahl, 1955)</li><li><strong>Common names:</strong> Schultz's Bumblebee Catfish, Schultz's Jelly Catfish</li><li><strong>Type locality:</strong> Cereté, Colombia</li><li><strong>Synonym:</strong> Zungaro zungaro schultzi</li><li><strong>Size:</strong> 207 mm (8.1 in) SL</li><li><strong>Identification:</strong> Broad dark brown stripe in the caudal fin; originates in Colombia.</li><li><strong>Etymology:</strong> Greek pseudes = false + pimele = fat + odous = teeth, i.e. 'false pimelodus'.</li></ul>"
